pen but getting dearer.**\n- Norvane Utilities priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably in Q3 2026. Its 2027 capex is planned up 12%.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, so funding costs are rising.\n- Debt probably can't cover the whole gap for the weaker borrowers. The documents don't say why.\n\n**Equity (n6.r1): weak.**\n- Pellham, the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. Its 2027 capex is planned up 18%.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size, and the Q3 credit report calls equity markets \"less receptive\".\n- Smaller offerings may still get done, but at a discount and in lower volume.\n\n**Result by utility:**\n- **Norvane:** likely able to fund its plan through debt.\n- **Pellham:** it is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". Its 2027 spending will probably come in below plan.\n\n**Implication:** Orders from stronger-credit utilities look more resilient than orders from Pellham. This matters for grid-equipment demand (n2) and for the VLTX question (n1).","ttft_ms":1251,"type":"result","duration_ms":36245,"uuid":"f58055e6-8b34-4cc8-a8d9-bbd529a32b3a","ttft_stream_ms":844,"time_to_request_ms":125,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":29,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":9,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":4,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":4,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":1,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":12,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":69,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":187,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":112,"proc